<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Delft</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">3 July 1428</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hook-and-cod-wars">Hook and Cod wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delft">Delft</a>, concluded on 3 July 1428, ended the main phase of the war between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacqueline-countess-of-hainaut">Jacqueline of Bavaria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-the-good">Philip the Good</a>, duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a>, over Hainaut, Holland and Zeeland. Jacqueline kept her titles, but Philip became her heir and governor, and she promised not to remarry without his consent. When she did, she had to give up her counties to him in 1433.</p></div>
